ic charge stored in it.)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/58e63a272902fbe1b948c923252e70e210ca4c60.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/a50d12bc3a0cec464155fd277fe4c221a1b422a0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/19983ae101117d7cb252b68a7552f34d9744e4c1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/645772d5f4be109232a783bee7a4d5cb3e9b2481.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/6e4a94a644e50a8c3428b7fc0c61821b3120a888.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, d)</p>","subject":"multi | Marks +1"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two concentric spherical shells carry equal and opposite uniformly charge <em>Q </em>is distributed over their surfaces are shown in below figure,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f6c4f8848cc924ccc16c4756b3e55a5b9d4d4801.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The electric field on the surface of the inner shell will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>zero</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/5ca2d643e7f6d7e85adfeca0a9a6efcf8f6598ef.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/80588b42853d4621ca74cbf783be6d59fa053476.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/3609cf692ba1bba21a8ae6a020b2321aea270741.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/b490d84433d2755d281fe0594ccbb4546ec13d0e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two uniformly and similarly charged circular rings and a field point <em>P </em>are shown in figure. If the field at <em>P </em>is zero, then the ratio of the charge densities on the rings <em>A </em>and <em>B </em>will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2ccda2776ede6689241ad7886b605809d3cf1a10.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>1 : 1</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>3 : 4</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>4 : 3</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>16 : 9</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>Let the rings <em>A </em>and <em>B </em>respectively have charges &lambda; and &lambda;&prime; (per unit length). As the resultant field at <em>P </em>is to be zero, the magnitude of the field due to each ring should be the same</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a4b6617446a725031f2b7c97c73e0d0900953584.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/fd409da917fed1157e64b8858f244daa1f795931.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two positive charges <em>Q </em>coulomb each are placed at points (0, 0, 0) and (2, 2, 0), while two negative charges <em>Q </em>coulomb each in magnitude are placed at points (0, 2, 0) and (2, 0, 0). The electric field at the point (1, 1, 0) is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>zero</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/088ffd1ff649110ef7182b4b3140e404c08545e9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/da89885333003c9c09dc1097e088e5a810b08111.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/064c8389e575a96e292091f53e0e761b234c78b3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>The two positive charges Q are diagonally opposite in position and at the same distance from the point (1, 1, 0). Fields produced by them are equal and opposite and so their resultant field is zero.<br />Similarly, the two negative charges at the diagonally opposite corners produce zero field due to mutual cancellation.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/05f012f00812d2d813fdb0a214db1137d0f41428.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:09.383Z"}